<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's real wages rise 5.5 pct yr/yr in H1.</title>
<headline>Hungary's real wages rise 5.5 pct yr/yr in H1.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average real wage of full-time epmloyees in Hungary rose 5.5 percent in the first half of the year from the same period of 1996, the Central Statistical Office (KSH) said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>Gross real wages increased 23.4 percent, KSH said.</p>
<p>The average wage for public employees rose by 25.6 percent, but wage growth in that sector slowed to 20.2 percent in the second quarter of the year from 31.8 percent in the first quarter, KSH said.</p>
<p>The average monthly gross wage was 53,020 ($267.71) forints in the first six months of 1997, the KSH said.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
